\\subsection\{Ablation Study\}\
\\label\{sec:ablation\}\
\
\
\\paragraph\{Overthinking-mitigating rescaling ablation.\}\
Table~\\ref\{tab:overthinking_ablation\} ablates answer-ready step detection and\
fixed post-ready scaling. The w/o post-ready scaling variant keeps the answer-ready criterion but removes fixed post-ready rescaling by setting\
$\\gamma_\{\\mathrm\{post\}\}^\{+\}=\\gamma_\{\\mathrm\{post\}\}^\{-\}=1$, leading to\
substantially longer responses and lower accuracy. The w/o answer-ready step\
variant applies utility-guided rescaling to all selected reflective steps;\
although responses remain short, accuracy drops because the distinction between\
potentially useful pre-ready reflection and redundant post-ready continuation is\
removed. Full \\textsc\{RUAR\} combines these two components: the answer-ready\
step identifies where fine-grained utility estimation should stop, while fixed\
post-ready scaling suppresses further continuation. Its average scaling factors\
are therefore shifted in the intended direction, reducing positive credit and\
increasing negative penalties. Additional component and sensitivity analyses are\
provided in Appendices~\\ref\{app:component_ablation\}\
and~\\ref\{app:sensitivity_analyses\}.\
